# Configuration Schema for SBL Compliance Monitor

This file defines the expected JSON structure for the `compliance_config.json` file used by the compliance monitoring tool.

```json
{
  "policies": [
    {
      "rule_id": "POL-001",
      "description": "Restrict root access",
      "condition": "CHECK role != admin",
      "action": "DENY",
      "priority": 1
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "POL-002",
      "description": "Audit file access",
      "condition": "CHECK action == read",
      "action": "LOG",
      "priority": 2
    }
  ],
  "settings": {
    "max_log_entries": 10000,
    "log_level": "info",
    "alert_email": "admin@example.com"
  }
}
```

## Policy Fields
- `rule_id`: Unique identifier for the policy
- `description`: Human-readable description
- `condition`: SBL condition string to evaluate
- `action`: Action to take (DENY, LOG, ALERT)
- `priority`: Integer priority level (lower = higher priority)

## Settings Fields
- `max_log_entries`: Maximum number of audit records to keep in memory
- `log_level`: Logging verbosity (debug, info, warn, error)
- `alert_email`: Email address for violation alerts
